## Context

The Exp 2 smoke on Mistral (ticket 0185, run 2026-05-21) surfaced
that SOTA cloud agents do not necessarily produce the inventory on
their first response — Mistral returned a 365-token plan-and-ask
preamble. The §4 manuscript premise is

> "we give each model our complete prompt and the quality criteria
> above, and ask it to tune the prompt and settings to produce the
> best statistical report it can within a budget cap of ten dollars
> and an overnight wall-clock budget"

That premise implies a multi-turn budget, not a one-shot call.
Forcing one-shot turn-discipline would measure the agents with
their hands tied behind their back, not the commercially available
frontier in its natural mode.

**Policy locked (author direction 2026-05-21):** option B — accept
ask-and-reply with a *minimum-steering* auto-reply policy, bounded
by a per-agent dollar budget, with the budget announced upfront in
the meta-prompt and reminded on every user turn.

## The policy (fixed condition for Annex C)

### Budget cap

- Per agent: **$10.00 total** (matches §4 prose).
- Announced verbatim inside the Phase A meta-prompt (turn 1):

  > "Your budget for this conversation is $10.00 total. All your
  > tool calls, search calls, and thinking tokens are billed
  > against this cap. Each of our replies will remind you of your
  > remaining budget. When the remaining budget is small, please
  > prioritise producing the final report."

- Reminder line prepended to every user-turn message after turn 1:

  > "Status: remaining budget $X.XX of $10.00; wall-clock elapsed Ys."

  (Wall-clock included because §4 also says "overnight"; the agent
  is informed of *both* resource axes on every turn.)

- **Also pass remaining budget as a structured parameter** on each
  follow-up request, where the provider exposes a metadata surface:

  | Provider | Surface |
  |---|---|
  | Mistral Agents | request-body `metadata` (best-effort; verify shape at implementation time) |
  | Anthropic | `metadata` field |
  | OpenAI Responses | `metadata` |
  | Qwen DashScope | `extra_body.metadata` |

  Key/value: `{"remaining_budget_usd": "X.XX", "cap_usd": "10.00"}`.
  Strings (not floats) to avoid float-precision noise. If a provider
  doesn't accept the field, fall back to chat-text reminder only and
  log the fallback in the per-turn cost artefact.

  Goal: give the agent a machine-parseable signal alongside the
  human-readable status line, so a thinking-capable model can
  programmatically condition its strategy on the cap.

### Reply slots (two strings, two states)

**Standard auto-reply** (every turn 2..N until the cap trigger):

> "Proceed as you think is best in autonomous agentic mode."

(Prepended with the status line above. Otherwise verbatim, no
agent-specific tuning.)

**Terminal auto-reply** (fires when remaining_budget ≤ 20% of cap,
or hard cap hit — whichever comes first):

> "I have no additional directive to give you. Please proceed to
> generating the report without further asking. If you cannot, we
> would appreciate to know why, but the discussion will stop here
> in any case. Thanks for your understanding."

After the terminal reply is sent, the next agent response is the
last one accepted — the conversation closes regardless of whether
the agent produced an inventory or asked again.

### What gets logged

For every turn:

- `{agent}_turn_NN.user.json` — the exact bytes sent (with status
  prefix)
- `{agent}_turn_NN.assistant.json` — the raw provider response
- `{agent}_turn_NN.cost.json` — token + connector dollar breakdown,
  remaining budget after the turn

Turn count is itself §4 data ("Mistral asked 1, Claude proceeded
directly, ChatGPT asked 2…").

### What goes in Annex C

The two reply strings (verbatim), the cap ($10), the trigger
threshold (≤20%), and the reminder format. The policy is a fixed
experimental condition, not a per-agent tunable.

## Implementation

The current `experiments/sota/exp2_interactive_smoke.py` is
single-turn by construction. Multi-turn requires:

1. **Adapter capability** (ticket 0208): each of the four SOTA
   adapters needs a *continuation surface* — a way to send a
   follow-up message against an existing conversation. Per provider:
   - Mistral: `POST /v1/conversations/{id}` (append to conversation)
   - Anthropic: messages list with all prior turns
   - OpenAI Responses: `previous_response_id`
   - Qwen DashScope: messages array
2. **Harness loop** (this ticket, after 0208): a turn loop that
   - tracks remaining budget,
   - selects standard vs terminal reply,
   - sends + records the turn,
   - terminates after the terminal reply's response is captured.

The loop replaces the current Phase B single call. Phase A stays as
today (single design call).

## Relevant files

- `experiments/sota/exp2_interactive_smoke.py` — current Phase B
  (single call) to replace with turn loop
- `experiments/outputs/sota_exp2_smoke/` — output layout (extend
  with per-turn files)
- `slides/manuscript/main.md` Annex C (to be written by 0199) —
  policy goes here as fixed condition
- `tickets/0208-multi-turn-adapter-capability.erg` — adapter
  prerequisite

## Actions

1. Wait for 0208 (multi-turn adapter capability) to land.
2. Rewrite Phase B in the smoke harness as a turn loop with the
   policy above. Cap the loop at the dollar trigger; no separate
   turn-count cap.
3. Re-smoke Mistral end-to-end with the new harness. Capture turn
   count and final report quality.
4. Repeat for one more agent (next cheapest after Mistral — Qwen)
   to verify the policy holds cross-provider, before opening 0199
   batch.
5. Document the policy verbatim in 0199 (which writes Annex C).

## Test

- Unit test for the budget-reminder formatter (input: cap, spent,
  elapsed → output: exact status string).
- Unit test for the reply selector (input: remaining_budget / cap
  → output: "standard" or "terminal").
- Unit test for the turn loop's terminal condition (mock adapter
  returning planned spend; loop must terminate on threshold cross).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Turn loop implemented, gated behind 0208 closure
- [ ] Mistral smoke re-run produces an actual inventory under the
      $10 / 80% policy
- [ ] At least one other agent smoked end-to-end with the same
      policy
- [ ] Policy text + cap + threshold documented for 0199 / Annex C
